{"id": "803e35eb-c66f-4291-abee-06d63aad65d5", "text": "Q: Is there a version of MySQL connector for Python 3.9? A: <p>User <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/users/7779049/nuno-mariz\">Nuno Mariz</a> <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/65925851/mysql-connector-for-python-3-9#comment117170863_65925851\">commented</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The support for Python 3.9 will be added in the upcoming Connector/Python 8.0.24 that will be released soon. Nonetheless Connector/Python 8.0.22/23 works with Python 3.9, only the metadata in packaging doesn't comply</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>So while mysql-connector-python page on pypi did not assert compatibility with Python 3.9 at the time of asking, v. 8.0.22/23 would still work if installed under Python 3.9.</p>\n", "tags": ["python", "mysql-python", "mysql-connector"]}
{"id": "3c372d70-a051-4e79-afc7-577148edb0b7", "text": "Q: Scan directories and copy those that have more than n files A: <p>This seems to do the job!</p>\n<p>Do you see issues with the below?</p>\n<pre><code>import os\nimport shutil\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsource = Path(&quot;./music/&quot;)\ndest = Path(&quot;./musiclight/&quot;)\nthreshold = 7\n\nos.makedirs(dest, exist_ok=True)\n\nfor artist in source.iterdir():\n    #print(f&quot;je traite : {artist.name}&quot;)\n    total_files = 0\n    if artist.is_dir():\n        for album in artist.iterdir():\n            if album.is_dir():\n                #print(f&quot;je traite : {artist.name} - {album.name}&quot;)\n                total_files += sum(1 for f in album.rglob('*') if f.is_file())\n        if total_files &gt;= threshold:\n            print(f&quot;Artist {artist.name} has {total_files} files - ABOVE threshold - To be copied&quot;)\n            shutil.copytree(artist, dest / artist.name, dirs_exist_ok=True)\n        else:\n            print(f&quot;Artist {artist.name} has {total_files} files - BELOW threshold - Ignoring&quot;)\n</code></pre>\n", "tags": ["python"]}
{"id": "76324250-727e-4a7e-bc25-c0a10a8bae35", "text": "Q: Why does my button work perfectly fine on desktop but not at all on my mobile browser? A: <p>first check mobile viewport and touch event behavior. Also inspect whether any parent element or CSS is blocking pointer events on mobile. Testing with browser mobile device emulator can help isolate whether it\u2019s CSS or click handler.</p>\n", "tags": ["reactjs", "next.js", "tailwind-css"]}
{"id": "49a861e0-d890-43c6-af6b-97dbe9dfa5c0", "text": "Q: PSQLException: The server requested password-based authentication, but no password was provided A: <p>The problem may be occured by beans scanning</p>\n<p>I have the same problem but logs did not indicate it.</p>\n<p>Try:</p>\n<pre><code>@Configuration\npublic class DataSourceConfig {\n    @Value(&quot;${spring.datasource.driver-class-name}&quot;)\n    private String driverClass;\n    @Value(&quot;${spring.datasource.data-username}&quot;)\n    private String url;\n    @Value(&quot;${spring.datasource.data-username}&quot;)\n    private String userName;\n    @Value(&quot;${spring.datasource.data-password}&quot;)\n    private String password;\n\n    @Bean\n    public DataSource getDataSource() {\n        return DataSourceBuilder.create()\n                .driverClassName(driverClass)\n                .url(url)\n                .username(userName)\n                .password(password)\n                .build();\n    }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>If you use SpringBoot, move to package with SpringBootApplication runner or define scanning manually</p>\n", "tags": ["java", "spring", "postgresql"]}
{"id": "5b91905d-6823-47af-9691-37d1be415f1f", "text": "Q: Set value in a datagridview cell programmatically A: <pre><code>DataGridViewTextBoxColumn column = new DataGridViewTextBoxColumn();\ncolumn.Name = \"DeclaredBy\";\ncolumn.HeaderText = \"DeclaredBy\";\ndataGridView1.Columns.Add(column);\ndataGridView1.Rows.Add(\"test value\");\ndataGridView1.Rows[0].Cells[\"DeclaredBy\"].Value = \"changed test value\";\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>This is working. Try on newly created <code>DataGridView</code>, without any columns at all. If that will work, probably you made some changes on your <code>DataGridView</code> that disallow changing value. Ofc, when you run this, you will see only <code>\"changed test value\"</code>, but this is also working, when the last line is under another button. Another possible solution is that maybe your <code>i</code> is not the one you want to.</p>\n", "tags": ["c#", "datagridview"]}
{"id": "269156f1-a22c-4b55-af04-e9e8f7f731db", "text": "Q: how to get auto-populate fields in servicenow A: <p>So if I understand you correctly you want to display more Information about the Caller in the Incident Form is that right?\nIf so you have a few possibilities: </p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Since Caller is a reference field you can just put the fields on the form via form designer and make them read-only with a UI-Policy.</li>\n<li>On every Reference field you have a reference icon, you get a preview when you hover over that icon. You could use this functionality to display the additional fields.</li>\n<li>You could write a UI-Macro that displays the additional fields.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Or you create custom fields on the Incident and populate them like you are doing in your snippet, but than I would ask what exactly is your Question?</p>\n", "tags": ["servicenow"]}
{"id": "7e0dd9d9-ffa5-4932-a60c-fac0095cd60e", "text": "Q: Read XML response webservice A: <p>You should just try deleting the service reference, rerun the service, and on the client add service reference.</p>\n", "tags": ["c#", "webservice-client"]}
{"id": "cf25aa6e-7975-479e-9ac7-8db838e8c299", "text": "Q: What is the optimized regex to match the email pattern in java A: <p>This absolutely not possible and your regex will miss a LOT. The email standard is a lot more flexible than you realize and while allowing a very limited subset for your own business logic can be covered with a relatively simple regex, the version you have now shows you already need more than that.</p>\n<p>Let me show you what it looks like when a library is dedicated to parsing/validating email addresses and <em>still</em> failed at it: <a href=\"https://github.com/bbottema/email-rfc2822-validator/blob/master/src/main/java/org/hazlewood/connor/bottema/emailaddress/Dragons.java\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/bbottema/email-rfc2822-validator/blob/master/src/main/java/org/hazlewood/connor/bottema/emailaddress/Dragons.java</a>. I inherited and used to maintain this library for my other open source library, <a href=\"https://www.simplejavamail.org/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">Simple Java Mail</a>, but we gave up immediately once a proper open source lexer library became available. Simple Java Mail provides <a href=\"https://simplejavamail.org/features.html#section-email-validation\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">email validation</a> through this.</p>\n<p>Here's the 'comprehensive' compiled regex that is the result of the 'common' parsing validation/configuration flags combination (it even works!):</p>\n<pre><code>/* HERE BE DRAGONS: The current regex string for mailbox token, just for fun:\n(((?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\n\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x\n0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))|(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)))?[a-zA-Z0\n-9!#-'*+\\-/=?^-`{-~.\\[]]+(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~\n]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)\n?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))|(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[\n \\t]+)))?)|(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x0\n1-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\n\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))|(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)))?&quot;(\n?&gt;(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?(?:[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!#-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F])))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[\n\\t]+)?&quot;(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\\nx0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0\nC\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))|(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)))?))(?:(?:(\n?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]\n-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]\n+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))|(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)\n?[ \\t]+)))?[a-zA-Z0-9!#-'*+\\-/=?^-`{-~.\\[]]+(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\n\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:\n[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))|\n(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)))?)|(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'\n*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)\n?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))|(?:(?:[ \\t]\n*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)))?&quot;(?&gt;(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?(?:[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!#-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F])))*(\n?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?&quot;(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-\n~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+\n)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))|(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?\n[ \\t]+)))?)))*)??((?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\\n[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\))*(?:(?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?\\((?:(?:(?:[ \\t]*\\r\\n)?[ \\t]+)?[\\x01-\n\\x08\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x1F\\x7F!-'*-\\[\\]-~]|(?:\\\\[\\x01-\\x09\\x0B\\x0C\\x0E-\\x7F]))*(?:(?: